  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Server Launch**\n\nI\'m focusing on the server\'s launch configuration. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant scripts in `package.json`. The development server starts with `tsx server.ts`, builds with Vite, and starts the production server with `node server`. I will ensure port 3000 is correctly configured and utilized for our Express + Vite + WebSocket setup.\n\n\n**Refining Server Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing `/server.ts`. It will be an Express server running on port 3000, dynamically serving Vite middleware in development and static `dist` files in production. Crucially, I\'m setting up a proxy route (`/api/nxsha/feed`) that fetches and transforms data from `nxsha.space`, merging it with seed items for offline functionality. I\'m also preparing for Gemini API endpoints using `@google/genai`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Gemini API Usage**\n\nI\'m structuring the Gemini API calls. For detailed analysis, I\'ll leverage `gemini-4-argon` if available, gracefully falling back to `gemini-3.8-flash` if there are billing or API key permission issues. I am also implementing a recommendation endpoint (`/api/gemini/recommend`) using `gemini-3.8-flash` for personalized suggestions and a recap endpoint (`/api/gemini/quick-recap`) with `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for rapid scene summaries. Finally, I\'ll establish a `/ws/party` path for real-time WebSocket communication, supporting multi-room watch parties.\n\n\n**Implementing WebSocket Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating WebSocket functionality within the server. I\'m focusing on features such as joining rooms (`mode: \'group\' | \'couple\'`), synchronization of play/pause/seek events, real-time chat messages, and implementing couple-specific features like heartbeat pulses and shared notes. I\'ve pre-seeded two rooms: `room-nxsha-prime` and `couple-lounge-77`, for immediate user access. Furthermore, I\'m setting up a `/ws/live` path for a real-time Gemini Live API bridge, using `gemini-3.8-live` to manage voice conversations with audio stream forwarding. I am thinking I need to create the files `/server.ts`, `/src/data/catalog.ts`, and `/src/components/MediaPoster.tsx`.\n\n\n"
