  planner_response {
    response: "I have created **Nxsha Stream**, a cross-platform streaming application and Watch Party platform powered by `https://nxsha.space`.\n\n### Key Capabilities Built & Verified\n- **Unified Catalog & `nxsha.space` Feed Integration**: Connects to `https://nxsha.space/api/home-feed` on the server with multi-platform filtering (*Nxsha Originals, Netflix, Prime Video, Disney+, Crunchyroll, Max*), category filters (*Movies, TV Series, Anime*), and instant multi-field search.\n- **Adaptive Bitrate (ABR) Video Engine**: Supports automatic and manual quality switching (*4K UHD 18.4 Mbps AV1, 1080p FHD 6.8 Mbps HEVC, 720p HD, and 480p Data Saver*), live link-speed simulation, subtitle tracks, and a direct switcher between the **Adaptive Stream** engine and the **`nxsha.space` Cloud Player**.\n- **Group Watch Party & 2-Seat Couple Watch Party Lounge**: Real-time WebSocket synchronization (`/ws/party`) with frame-locked playback, drift monitoring, timestamped room chat, and a dedicated **Couple Watch Party Lounge** featuring a strict 2-seat encrypted room, shared heartbeat pulses, and a shared date-night pinboard.\n- **Offline Playback Vault**: Download titles in selectable bitrates with storage quota tracking and an interactive **Simulate Offline Mode** switch for playback without internet connectivity.\n- **Social Broadcasts, Security & Push Notifications**: Broadcast timestamped clips to the Community Feed, X/Twitter, Discord, Telegram, or Couple Notes; manage End-to-End Encrypted Viewing History, Incognito Sessions, and DRM Couple PIN locks; and receive Episode & Trending Release push alerts.\n- **Gemini Intelligence & Live Voice Companion**:\n  - **High-Thinking Cinema Analyst (`gemini-4-argon` with `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`)** for deep thematic and narrative analysis.\n  - **Personalized Recommendation Curator (`gemini-3.8-flash`)** driven by viewing history and genre affinity weights.\n  - **Instant Scene Recap (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite`)** for spoiler-free context at the current video timestamp.\n  - **Real-Time Voice Companion (`gemini-3.8-live`)** via WebSocket (`/ws/live`) for conversational discovery.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: Verified 6 test suites in `streamEngine.test.ts` covering adaptive bitrate selection, watch-history recommendation scoring, Watch Party drift reconciliation, multi-field catalog search, offline storage quota calculations, and E2EE privacy fingerprints (`6 passed, 0 failed`).\n- **Browser & Viewport Verification**: Verified desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) layouts across Discover, Couple Watch Party Lounge, AI & Voice Companion, and Offline & Social Vault with zero console errors. (Note: Since paid API key setup was declined, `gemini-4-argon` automatically falls back when a paid key is not attached.)"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Scenario**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the implications of the provided images, specifically `r2-couple.png`, `r2-ai.png`, and `r2-mobile.png`. It seems like the core concept revolves around secure, real-time collaboration with E2EE, potentially for couples or duos, as suggested by \"2 / 2 Seats Occupied\" and \"Active Roster\". The \"WebSocket synced with 0\" is something I must consider carefully in this real-time system.\n\n\n"
