  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Installing Dependencies**\n\nOkay, I\'ve moved past the initial setup and am now focusing on installing essential packages. I\'m following `cloudsql-setup` instructions closely, specifically focusing on `Step 4.2` and `Step 5.1.1`. Currently, I am installing `firebase`, both the Client and Admin SDKs, and also including `drizzle-orm` in the setup.\n\n\n**Adding Applet Packages**\n\nOkay, the installation is underway, and I\'ve initiated `install_applet_package` for `firebase`, `firebase-admin`, `drizzle-orm`, `drizzle-kit`, `pg`, `@types/pg`, and `react-router-dom`. While that\'s progressing, I\'m now crafting the `Firebase Auth` files (`src/lib/firebase.ts`, `src/lib/firebase-admin.ts`, `src/middleware/auth.ts`) and Drizzle setup files (`src/db/schema.ts`, `src/db/drizzle.config.ts`, `src/db/index.ts`, `src/db/users.ts`), ensuring strict adherence to the `cloudsql-setup` instructions. Specifically, `src/lib/firebase.ts` is coming together, closely mirroring the defined code.\n\n\n**Defining Core Imports**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the necessary imports. I\'ve integrated the mandatory static JSON import for `firebaseConfig` within the setup. Also, I\'m creating the core authentication middleware by defining `requireAuth` and `optionalAuth` which I believe will enable seamless guest/demo user functionality, as well as authenticated private room mutations on the server. I am also working on creating the `src/db/schema.ts` file including all the tables, as outlined in the provided prompt.\n\n\n**Constructing Database Tables**\n\nOkay, I\'m defining the database schema, focusing on the tables outlined. I\'m adding fields for various data points: room details (`currentMediaId`, `currentMediaType`, etc.), and user states (`isPrivate`, `passwordHash`). I\'m now structuring the relationships within the schema to support `room_members`, `playback_states`, `chat_messages`, `room_reactions`, `room_votes`, and `watch_sessions`. I\'m using appropriate data types and primary key definitions for each column.\n\n\n"
