ard, and \"Next Movie?\" voting queue.\n  - **Mode B \342\200\224 Friends & Group Cinema \360\237\216\211**:\n    - Configurable 3\342\200\22320 participant capacity, host vs. collaborative playback control toggle, room lock/unlock toggle, host transfer, participant removal, group movie voting, and optional WebRTC voice/video lounge controls (`Mic Mute/Unmute`, `Hold PTT`, `Camera On/Off`).\n\n- **Multi-Session Real-Time WebSocket & Cloud SQL Persistence (Verified with Two Independent Browser Sessions)**:\n  - Verified with two independent Playwright browser sessions (`host` and `partner`):\n    - **Session 1 (`host`)** created room `LOVE-WWMB` via `POST /api/party/rooms` (persisted in Cloud SQL `watch_rooms` and `playback_states`).\n    - **Session 2 (`partner`)** joined via the invite link `/?room=LOVE-WWMB&mode=couple`, updated the room lifecycle state to `Partner joined`, and sent real-time chat (`\"Hello from Browser Session 2 in LOVE-WWMB! \342\235\244\357\270\217\"`) and a `\342\235\244\357\270\217` reaction, which immediately appeared in Session 1 and persisted in Cloud SQL `chat_messages` and `room_reactions`.\n\n- **`MediaProviderAdapter` & Honest External Embed Integration**:\n  - Implemented `MediaProviderAdapter` with two concrete adapters:\n    1. **`SyncedStudioVideoAdapter`**: Full programmatic `play()`, `pause()`, `seekTo()`, `getCurrentTime()`, `getDuration()`, and WebSocket revision-ordered drift reconciliation (`shouldAcceptSyncRevision`, `classifyPlaybackDrift`).\n    2. **`NxshaExternalEmbedAdapter`**: Builds `/embed/movie/{tmdbId}` and `/embed/tv/{tmdbId}/{season}/{episode}` with dynamic Season & Episode selectors, explicitly sets `supportsProgrammaticSync = false`, displays the honest cross-origin limitation banner (`[data-testid=\"external-sync-limitation-banner\"]`), and provides a **3-2-1 Manual Room Countdown** overlay for manual coordination.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Known Limitations\n\n- **Cross-Origin Third-Party Iframe Synchronization**:\n  - Third-party embeds (`https://nxsha.space/embed/movie/{id}` and `/embed/tv/{id}/{season}/{episode}`) run inside cross-origin iframes that do not expose postMessage or DOM `HTMLMediaElement` hooks for programmatic `play`/`pause`/`seekTo`. When a room switches to **External Embed (/embed)** mode, automatic WebSocket seek/play lockstep is disabled and replaced by the **3-2-1 Manual Room Countdown** and timestamp coordination banner.\n- **Sandbox Camera/Microphone Hardware**:\n  - In headless browser or restricted iframe environments without physical audio/video capture devices, the WebRTC voice/video controls gracefully fall back to room signaling presence without crashing.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Environment Variables (`.env.example`)\n\n| Variable | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Server-side API key for Gemini Film Theorist & Curator endpoints (`/api/gemini/*`) |\n| `APP_URL` | Hosted application URL injected at runtime |\n| `VITE_APP_NAME` | Configurable brand name (defaults to `CineTogether`) |\n| `VITE_MEDIA_EMBED_BASE_URL` | Base URL for external media embeds (defaults to `https://nxsha.space`) |\n| `VITE_TMDB_API_KEY` | Optional TMDB API key for additional live metadata enrichment |\n| `VITE_WS_URL` | Optional custom WebSocket relay URL (defaults to same-origin `/ws/party`) |\n| `SQL_HOST` | Cloud SQL PostgreSQL host IP |\n| `SQL_DB_NAME` | Cloud SQL PostgreSQL database name (`postgres`) |\n| `SQL_USER` / `SQL_PASSWORD` | Application database credentials used by the Drizzle connection pool |\n| `SQL_ADMIN_USER` / `SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD` | Admin credentials used by `drizzle-kit` for schema migrations |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Exact Deployment Steps\n\n1. **Install Dependencies**:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n2. **Configure Environment Variables**:\n   Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and populate your PostgreSQL (`SQL_HOST`, `SQL_DB_NAME`, `SQL_USER`, `SQL_PASSWORD`) and `GEMINI_API_KEY` values.\n3. **Push Database Schema**:\n   Ensure the 11 PostgreSQL tables (`profiles`, `media_items`, `watch_rooms`, `watchlists`, `watchlist_items`, `room_members`, `playback_states`, `chat_messages`, `room_reactions`, `room_votes`, `watch_sessions`) are synced via Drizzle.\n4. **Run Unit Tests & Build Frontend Assets**:\n   ```bash\n   npx tsx --test src/utils/streamEngine.test.ts\n   npm run build\n   ```\n5. **Start the Production Server (Express + WebSocket `/ws/party` on Port 3000)**:\n   ```bash\n   NODE_ENV=production npx tsx server.ts\n   ```"
