  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a complete responsive movie watch-party website named CineTogether, inspired by the cinematic UI of https://aethoflix.world/ and the media discovery experience of https://nxsha.space/.\n\nUse React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.\n\nCreate two separate watch-party experiences:\n\n1. Couple Cinema \342\235\244\357\270\217 \342\200\224 private rooms for two people, romantic dark-purple theme, invite links, shared movie selection, real-time chat, emoji reactions, and synchronized playback when supported.\n2. Group Cinema \360\237\216\211 \342\200\224 rooms for up to 20 people, participant lists, invite links, real-time chat, host controls, movie voting, and synchronized playback when supported.\n\nCreate a premium streaming-style homepage with a hero banner, movie posters, trending titles, genres, search, movie details, watchlist, and a clear Create Watch Party button.\n\nUse demo movie data initially. Build working navigation, functional buttons, room creation, room joining, chat, and responsive layouts. Use Firebase or another suitable backend for persistent rooms and realtime communication.\n\nIntegrate Nxsha only through publicly documented and permitted interfaces. Do not invent APIs or assume third-party video links can be embedded or synchronized. Provide a provider adapter, playback capability detection, and an Open on Provider fallback when embedding is unavailable.\n\nMake the UI beautiful and the core features functional. Build the actual application, run it, fix errors, and show the working preview. Do not stop at a static design."
    items {
      text: "Build a complete responsive movie watch-party website named CineTogether, inspired by the cinematic UI of https://aethoflix.world/ and the media discovery experience of https://nxsha.space/.\n\nUse React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.\n\nCreate two separate watch-party experiences:\n\n1. Couple Cinema \342\235\244\357\270\217 \342\200\224 private rooms for two people, romantic dark-purple theme, invite links, shared movie selection, real-time chat, emoji reactions, and synchronized playback when supported.\n2. Group Cinema \360\237\216\211 \342\200\224 rooms for up to 20 people, participant lists, invite links, real-time chat, host controls, movie voting, and synchronized playback when supported.\n\nCreate a premium streaming-style homepage with a hero banner, movie posters, trending titles, genres, search, movie details, watchlist, and a clear Create Watch Party button.\n\nUse demo movie data initially. Build working navigation, functional buttons, room creation, room joining, chat, and responsive layouts. Use Firebase or another suitable backend for persistent rooms and realtime communication.\n\nIntegrate Nxsha only through publicly documented and permitted interfaces. Do not invent APIs or assume third-party video links can be embedded or synchronized. Provide a provider adapter, playback capability detection, and an Open on Provider fallback when embedding is unavailable.\n\nMake the UI beautiful and the core features functional. Build the actual application, run it, fix errors, and show the working preview. Do not stop at a static design."
    }
  }
}
